#: ../../source/references_other.md:99
msgid ""
"The generic join context manager facilitates distributed training on "
"uneven inputs. This page outlines the API of the relevant classes: Join, "
"Joinable, and JoinHook. For a tutorial, see Distributed Training with "
"Uneven Inputs Using the Join Context Manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:101
msgid ""
"This class defines the generic join context manager, which allows custom "
"hooks to be called after a process joins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:103
msgid ""
"These hooks should shadow the collective communications of non-joined "
"processes to prevent hanging and erroring and to ensure algorithmic "
"correctness. Refer to JoinHook for details about the hook definition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:105
msgid ""
"The context manager requires each participating Joinable to call the "
"method notify_join_context() before its own per- iteration collective "
"communications to ensure correctness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:107
msgid ""
"The context manager requires that all process_group attributes in the "
"JoinHook objects are the same. If there are multiple JoinHook objects, "
"then the device of the first is used. The process group and device "
"information is used for checking for non- joined processes and for "
"notifying processes to throw an exception if throw_on_early_termination "
"is enabled, both of which using an all- reduce."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:109
msgid ""
"joinables (List[Joinable]) – a list of the participating Joinable s; "
"their hooks are iterated over in the given order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:111
msgid ""
"enable (bool) – a flag enabling uneven input detection; setting to False "
"disables the context manager’s functionality and should only be set when "
"the user knows the inputs will not be uneven (default: True)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:113
msgid ""
"throw_on_early_termination (bool) – a flag controlling whether to throw "
"an exception upon detecting uneven inputs (default: False)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:115
msgid ""
"Notifies the join context manager that the calling process has not yet "
"joined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:117
msgid ""
"Then, if throw_on_early_termination=True, checks if uneven inputs have "
"been detected (i.e. if one process has already joined) and throws an "
"exception if so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:119
msgid ""
"This method should be called from a Joinable object before its per-"
"iteration collective communications. For example, this should be called "
"at the beginning of the forward pass in DistributedDataParallel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:121
msgid ""
"Only the first Joinable object passed into the context manager performs "
"the collective communications in this method, and for the others, this "
"method is vacuous."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:123
msgid "joinable (Joinable) – the Joinable object calling this method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:125
msgid ""
"An async work handle for the all-reduce meant to notify the context "
"manager that the process has not yet joined if joinable is the first one "
"passed into the context manager; None otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:127
msgid "This defines an abstract base class for joinable classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:129
msgid ""
"A joinable class (inheriting from Joinable) should implement join_hook(),"
" which returns a JoinHook instance, in addition to join_device() and "
"join_process_group() that return device and process group information, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:131
msgid ""
"Return the device from which to perform collective communications needed "
"by the join context manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:133
msgid "Return a JoinHook instance for the given Joinable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:135 ../../source/references_other.md:1919
#: ../../source/references_other.md:3825
msgid ""
"kwargs (dict) – a dict containing any keyword arguments to modify the "
"behavior of the join hook at run time; all Joinable instances sharing the"
" same join context manager are forwarded the same value for kwargs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:137
msgid ""
"Returns the process group for the collective communications needed by the"
" join context manager itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:139
msgid ""
"This defines a join hook, which provides two entry points in the join "
"context manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:141
msgid ""
"Entry points : a main hook, which is called repeatedly while there exists"
" a non-joined process, and a post-hook, which is called once all "
"processes have joined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:143
msgid ""
"To implement a join hook for the generic join context manager, define a "
"class that inherits from JoinHook and override main_hook() and "
"post_hook() as appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:145
msgid ""
"Call this hook while there exists a non-joined process to shadow "
"collective communications in a training iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:147
msgid ""
"Training iteration i.e., in one forward pass, backward pass, and "
"optimizer step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:149
msgid "Call hook after all processes have joined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:151
msgid ""
"It is passed an additional bool argument is_last_joiner, which indicates "
"if the rank is one of the last to join."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:153
msgid ""
"is_last_joiner (bool) – True if the rank is one of the last to join; "
"False otherwise."
msgstr ""

