#: ../../source/references_other.md:1979
msgid ""
"DDP communication hook is a generic interface to control how to "
"communicate gradients across workers by overriding the vanilla allreduce "
"in DistributedDataParallel. A few built-in communication hooks are "
"provided, and users can easily apply any of these hooks to optimize "
"communication. Besides, the hook interface can also support user-defined "
"communication strategies for more advanced use cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:1981
msgid ""
"To use a communication hook, the user just needs to let the DDP model "
"register the hook before the training loop as below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:1983
msgid "torch.nn.parallel.DistributedDataParallel.register_comm_hook()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:1985
msgid ""
"A communication hook provides a flexible way to allreduce gradients. "
"Therefore, it mainly operates on the gradients on each replica before "
"allreduce, which are bucketized to increase the overlap between "
"communication and computation. Particularly, torch.distributed.GradBucket"
" represents a bucket of gradient tensors to be allreduced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:1987
msgid ""
"This class mainly passes a flattened gradient tensor (returned by "
"buffer()) to DDP communication hook. This tensor can be further "
"decomposed into a list of per-parameter tensors within this bucket "
"(returned by get_per_parameter_tensors()) to apply layer-wise operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:1989
msgid ""
"Since the buckets are rebuilt after the first iteration, should not rely "
"on the indices at the beginning of training."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:1991
msgid ""
"The index of a bucket that stores gradients of a few contiguous layers. "
"All the gradients are bucketized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:1993
msgid ""
"A flattened 1D torch.Tensor buffer, which can be further decomposed into "
"a list of per-parameter tensors within this bucket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:1995
msgid "A list of torch.Tensor. Each tensor in the list corresponds to a gradient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:1997
msgid ""
"Whether this bucket is the last bucket to allreduce in an iteration. This"
" also means that this bucket corresponds to the first few layers in the "
"forward pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:1999
msgid "Replaces the tensor in the bucket with the input tensor buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2001
msgid ""
"A list of torch.Tensor. Each tensor in the list corresponds to a model "
"parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2003
msgid ""
"Default communication hooks are simple stateless hooks, so the input "
"state in register_comm_hook is either a process group or None. The input "
"bucket is a torch.distributed.GradBucket object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2005
msgid "Call allreduce using GradBucket tensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2007
msgid ""
"Once gradient tensors are aggregated across all workers, its then "
"callback takes the mean and returns the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2009
msgid ""
"If user registers this DDP communication hook, DDP results is expected to"
" be same as the case where no hook was registered. Hence, this won’t "
"change behavior of DDP and user can use this as a reference or modify "
"this hook to log useful information or any other purposes while "
"unaffecting DDP behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2011
msgid ""
"Compress by casting GradBucket to torch.float16 divided by process group "
"size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2013
msgid ""
"This DDP communication hook implements a simple gradient compression "
"approach that casts GradBucket tensor to half-precision floating-point "
"format (torch.float16) and then divides it by the process group size. It "
"allreduces those float16 gradient tensors. Once compressed gradient "
"tensors are allreduced, the chained callback decompress casts it back to "
"the input data type (such as float32)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2015 ../../source/references_other.md:2027
msgid ""
"Warning: This API is experimental, and it requires NCCL version later "
"than 2.9.6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2017
msgid ""
"This DDP communication hook implements a simple gradient compression "
"approach that casts GradBucket tensor to half-precision Brain floating "
"point format (torch.bfloat16) and then divides it by the process group "
"size. It allreduces those bfloat16 gradient tensors. Once compressed "
"gradient tensors are allreduced, the chained callback decompress casts it"
" back to the input data type (such as float32)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2019
msgid ""
"Additionally, a communication hook wrapper is provided to support "
"fp16_compress_hook() or bf16_compress_hook() as a wrapper, which can be "
"combined with other communication hooks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2021
msgid ""
"Cast input tensor to torch.float16, cast result of hook back to input "
"dtype."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2023
msgid ""
"This wrapper casts the input gradient tensor of a given DDP communication"
" hook to half-precision floating point format (torch.float16), and casts "
"the resulting tensor of the given hook back to the input data type, such "
"as float32. Therefore, fp16_compress_hook is equivalent to "
"fp16_compress_wrapper(allreduce_hook)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2025 ../../source/references_other.md:2033
msgid "Callable[[Any, GradBucket], Future[Tensor]]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2029
msgid ""
"This wrapper casts the input gradient tensor of a given DDP communication"
" hook to half-precision Brain floating point format (torch.bfloat16), and"
" casts the resulting tensor of the given hook back to the input data "
"type, such as float32."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2031
msgid ""
"Therefore, bf16_compress_hook is equivalent to "
"bf16_compress_wrapper(allreduce_hook)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2035
msgid ""
"PowerSGD (Vogels et al., NeurIPS 2019) is a gradient compression "
"algorithm, which can provide very high compression rates and accelerate "
"bandwidth-bound distributed training. This algorithm needs to maintain "
"both some hyperparameters and the internal state. Therefore, PowerSGD "
"communication hook is a stateful hook, and the user needs to provide a "
"state object defined as below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2037
msgid ""
"Store both the algorithm’s hyperparameters and internal state for all "
"gradients during training."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2039
msgid ""
"Particularly, matrix_approximation_rank and start_powerSGD_iter are the "
"main hyperparameters that should be tuned by the user. For performance, "
"we suggest to keep binary hyperparameters use_error_feedback and "
"warm_start on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2041
msgid ""
"matrix_approximation_rank controls the size of compressed low-rank "
"tensors, which determines the compression rate. The lower the rank, the "
"stronger the compression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2043
msgid ""
"1.1. If matrix_approximation_rank is too low, the full model quality will"
" need more training steps to reach or will never reach and yield loss in "
"accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2045
msgid ""
"1.2. The increase of matrix_approximation_rank can substantially increase"
" the computation costs of the compression, and the accuracy may not be "
"further improved beyond a certain matrix_approximation_rank threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2047
msgid ""
"To tune matrix_approximation_rank, we suggest to start from 1 and "
"increase by factors of 2 (like an exponential grid search, 1, 2, 4, …), "
"until a satisfactory accuracy is reached. Typically only a small value "
"1-4 is used. For some NLP tasks (as shown in Appendix D of the original "
"paper), this value has been increased to 32."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2049
msgid ""
"start_powerSGD_iter defers PowerSGD compression until step "
"start_powerSGD_iter, and vanilla allreduce runs prior to step "
"start_powerSGD_iter. This hybrid scheme of vanilla allreduce + PowerSGD "
"can effectively improve the accuracy, even a relatively small "
"matrix_approximation_rank is used. This is because that, the beginning of"
" training phase is usually very sensitive to inaccurate gradients, and "
"compressing gradients too early may make the training quickly take a "
"suboptimal trajectory, which can result in an irrecoverable impact on the"
" accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2051
#, python-format
msgid ""
"To tune start_powerSGD_iter, we suggest to start with 10% of total "
"training steps, and increase it until a satisfactory accuracy is reached."
" If there is a warm-up stage in the training, start_powerSGD_iter "
"typically should be no less than the number of warm-up steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2053
msgid ""
"min_compression_rate is the minimum compression rate required when a "
"layer is compressed. Due to the computation overheads incurred by the "
"compression, a tensor is worth compressing only if there can be "
"sufficient saving in bandwidth, where (num_rows + num_cols) * "
"matrix_approximation_rank * min_compression_rate < num_rows * num_cols. "
"If the specified compression rate threshold cannot be satisfied, the "
"tensor will be directly allreduced without compression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2055
msgid ""
"Compression statistics are logged every "
"compression_stats_logging_frequency iterations once PowerSGD compression "
"starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2057
msgid ""
"orthogonalization_epsilon can be a very small value (e.g., 1e-8) added to"
" every normalized matrix column in orthogonalization step, to prevent "
"div-by-zero error if any column has all 0s. If this can already be "
"prevented (e.g., by batch normalization), an epsilon of 0 is recommended "
"for accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2059
msgid ""
"batch_tensors_with_same_shape controls whether to compress and decompress"
" tensors with same shape in a batched operation to achieve higher "
"parallelism. Note that you should also increase the bucket size (i.e., "
"bucket_cap_mb arg in DDP constructor) to make more same-shaped tensors "
"appear in the same bucket, however this may reduce the overlap between "
"computation and communication, and increase the memory footprint due to "
"stacking the tensors of the same shape. Set to True if the compression / "
"decompression computation is a bottleneck."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2061
msgid ""
"If error feedback or warm-up is enabled, the minimum value of "
"start_powerSGD_iter allowed in DDP is 2. This is because there is another"
" internal optimization that rebuilds buckets at iteration 1 in DDP, and "
"this can conflict with any tensor memorized before the rebuild process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2063
msgid ""
"PowerSGD typically requires extra memory of the same size as the model’s "
"gradients to enable error feedback, which can compensate for biased "
"compressed communication and improve accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2065
msgid ""
"PowerSGD hooks may conflict with Apex automatic mixed precision package. "
"Please use PyTorch native automatic mixed precision package instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2067
msgid "Implement PowerSGD algorithm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2069
msgid ""
"This DDP communication hook implements PowerSGD gradient compression "
"algorithm described in the paper. Once gradient tensors are aggregated "
"across all workers, this hook applies compression as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2071
msgid ""
"Views the input flattened 1D gradient tensor as a list of per-parameter "
"tensors, and divides all the tensors into two groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2073
msgid ""
"1.1 The tensors that should be compressed before allreduce, because the "
"compression can give enough saving in bandwidth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2075
msgid ""
"1.2 Rest of the tensors will be directly allreduced without compression, "
"including all the vector tensors (for biases)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2077
msgid "Handles uncompressed tensors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2079
msgid ""
"2.1. Allocate contiguous memory for those uncompressed tensors, and "
"allreduces all the uncompressed tensors as a batch, without compression;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2081
msgid ""
"2.2. Copies the individual uncompressed tensors from the contiguous "
"memory back to the input tensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2083
msgid "Handles the tensors that should be compressed by PowerSGD compression:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2085
msgid ""
"3.1. For each tensor M, creates two low-rank tensors P and Q for "
"decomposing M, such that M = PQ^T, where Q is initialized from a standard"
" normal distribution and orthogonalized;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2087
msgid "3.2. Computes each P in Ps, which is equal to MQ;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2089
msgid "3.3. Allreduces Ps as a batch;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2091
msgid "3.4. Orthogonalizes each P in Ps;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2093
msgid "3.5. Computes each Q in Qs, which is approximately equal to M^TP;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2095
msgid "3.6. Allreduces Qs as a batch;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2097
msgid ""
"3.7. Computes each M among all the compressed tensors, which is "
"approximately equal to PQ^T."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2099 ../../source/references_other.md:2127
msgid ""
"Note that this communication hook enforces vanilla allreduce for the "
"first state.start_powerSGD_iter iterations. This not only gives the user "
"more control over the tradeoff between speedup and accuracy, but also "
"helps abstract away some complexity of the internal optimization of DDP "
"for future communication hook developers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2101
msgid ""
"state (PowerSGDState) – State information to configure the compression "
"rate and support error feedback, warm start, etc. To tune the compression"
" configs, mainly need to tune matrix_approximation_rank, "
"start_powerSGD_iter and min_compression_rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2103 ../../source/references_other.md:2131
msgid ""
"bucket (dist.GradBucket) – Bucket that stores a 1D flattened gradient "
"tensor that batches multiple per-variable tensors. Note that since DDP "
"comm hook only supports single process single device mode, only exactly "
"one tensor is stored in this bucket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2105 ../../source/references_other.md:2133
msgid "Future handler of the communication, which updates the gradients in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2107
msgid "Implement simplified PowerSGD algorithm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2109
msgid ""
"This DDP communication hook implements a simplified PowerSGD gradient "
"compression algorithm described in the paper. This variant does not "
"compress the gradients layer by layer, but instead compresses the "
"flattened input tensor that batches all the gradients. Therefore, it is "
"faster than powerSGD_hook(), but usually results in a much lower "
"accuracy, unless matrix_approximation_rank is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2111
msgid ""
"Increasing matrix_approximation_rank here may not necessarily increase "
"the accuracy, because batching per-parameter tensors without column/row "
"alignment can destroy low-rank structure. Therefore, the user should "
"always consider powerSGD_hook() first, and only consider this variant "
"when a satisfactory accuracy can be achieved when "
"matrix_approximation_rank is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2113
msgid ""
"Once gradient tensors are aggregated across all workers, this hook "
"applies compression as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2115
msgid ""
"Views the input flattened 1D gradient tensor as a square-shaped tensor M "
"with 0 paddings;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2117
msgid ""
"Creates two low-rank tensors P and Q for decomposing M, such that M = "
"PQ^T, where Q is initialized from a standard normal distribution and "
"orthogonalized;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2119
msgid "Computes P, which is equal to MQ;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2121
msgid "Computes Q, which is approximately equal to M^TP;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2123
msgid "Computes M, which is approximately equal to PQ^T."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2125
msgid "Truncates the input tensor to the original length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2129
msgid ""
"state (PowerSGDState) – State information to configure the compression "
"rate and support error feedback, warm start, etc. To tune the compression"
" configs, mainly need to tune matrix_approximation_rank and "
"start_powerSGD_iter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2135
msgid ""
"As the name implies, debugging communication hooks are only used for "
"debugging and performance optimization purpose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2137
msgid ""
"Debugging communication hooks do not necessarily output the correct "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:2139
msgid ""
"Return a future that wraps the input, so it is a no-op that does not "
