#: ../../source/references_other.md:3137 ../../source/references_other.md:3155
#: ../../source/references_other.md:3171 ../../source/references_other.md:3187
msgid "A DTensor object on each rank"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3109
msgid ""
"Returns a DTensor filled with the scalar value 1, with the shape defined "
"by the variable argument size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3111 ../../source/references_other.md:3141
#: ../../source/references_other.md:3159 ../../source/references_other.md:3175
msgid ""
"size (int...) – a sequence of integers defining the shape of the output "
"DTensor. Can be a variable number of arguments or a collection like a "
"list or tuple. E.g.: ones(1,2,3..) or ones([1,2,3..]) or ones((1,2,3..))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3125
msgid ""
"Returns a DTensor filled with uninitialized data. The shape of the "
"DTensor is defined by the variable argument size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3127
msgid ""
"size (int...) – a sequence of integers defining the shape of the output "
"DTensor. Can be a variable number of arguments or a collection like a "
"list or tuple. E.g.: empty(1,2,3..) or empty([1,2,3..]) or "
"empty((1,2,3..))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3129
msgid ""
"dtype (torch.dtype, optional) – the desired data type of returned "
"DTensor. Default: if None, uses a global default (see "
"torch.set_default_dtype()). layout (torch.layout, optional): the desired "
"layout of returned DTensor. Default: torch.strided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3139
