#: ../../source/references_other.md:3428
msgid "Return the full optimizer state-dict."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3430
msgid ""
"Consolidates the full optimizer state on rank 0 and returns it as a dict "
"following the convention of torch.optim.Optimizer.state_dict(), i.e. with"
" keys \"state\" and \"param_groups\". The flattened parameters in FSDP "
"modules contained in model are mapped back to their unflattened "
"parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3432
msgid ""
"This needs to be called on all ranks since it uses collective "
"communications. However, if rank0_only=True, then the state dict is only "
"populated on rank 0, and all other ranks return an empty dict."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3434
msgid ""
"Unlike torch.optim.Optimizer.state_dict(), this method uses full "
"parameter names as keys instead of parameter IDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3436
msgid ""
"Like in torch.optim.Optimizer.state_dict(), the tensors contained in the "
"optimizer state dict are not cloned, so there may be aliasing surprises. "
"For best practices, consider saving the returned optimizer state dict "
"immediately, e.g. using torch.save()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3438 ../../source/references_other.md:3492
#: ../../source/references_other.md:3506
msgid ""
"model (torch.nn.Module) – Root module (which may or may not be a "
"FullyShardedDataParallel instance) whose parameters were passed into the "
"optimizer optim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3442
msgid ""
"optim_input (Optional[Union[List[Dict[str, Any]], "
"Iterable[torch.nn.Parameter]]]) – Input passed into the optimizer optim "
"representing either a list of parameter groups or an iterable of "
"parameters; if None, then this method assumes the input was "
"model.parameters(). This argument is deprecated, and there is no need to "
"pass it in anymore. (Default: None)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3444
msgid ""
"rank0_only (bool) – If True, saves the populated dict only on rank 0; if "
"False, saves it on all ranks. (Default: True)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3446 ../../source/references_other.md:3554
msgid ""
"group (dist.ProcessGroup) – Model’s process group or None if using the "
"default process group. (Default: None)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:3448
