#: ../../source/references_other.md:4118 ../../source/references_other.md:4123
msgid "Tensor Parallelism - torch.distributed.tensor.parallel#"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4120
msgid "**URL:** https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/distributed.tensor.parallel.html"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4125
msgid "Created On: Jun 13, 2025 | Last Updated On: Jun 13, 2025"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4127
msgid ""
"Tensor Parallelism(TP) is built on top of the PyTorch DistributedTensor "
"(DTensor)[https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/torch/distributed/tensor/README.md]"
" and provides different parallelism styles: Colwise, Rowwise, and "
"Sequence Parallelism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4129
msgid "Tensor Parallelism APIs are experimental and subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4131
msgid "The entrypoint to parallelize your nn.Module using Tensor Parallelism is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4133
msgid ""
"Apply Tensor Parallelism in PyTorch by parallelizing modules or sub-"
"modules based on a user-specified plan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4135
msgid ""
"We parallelize module or sub_modules based on a parallelize_plan. The "
"parallelize_plan contains ParallelStyle, which indicates how user wants "
"the module or sub_module to be parallelized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4137
msgid ""
"User can also specify different parallel style per module fully qualified"
" name (FQN)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4139
msgid ""
"Note that parallelize_module only accepts a 1-D DeviceMesh, if you have a"
" 2-D or N-D DeviceMesh, slice the DeviceMesh to a 1-D sub DeviceMesh "
"first then pass to this API(i.e. device_mesh[\"tp\"])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4141
msgid "module (nn.Module) – Module to be parallelized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4143
msgid ""
"device_mesh (DeviceMesh, optional) – Object which describes the mesh "
"topology of devices for the DTensor. If not specified, the call must be "
"under a DeviceMesh context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4145
msgid ""
"parallelize_plan (Union[ParallelStyle, Dict[str, ParallelStyle]], "
"optional) – The plan used to parallelize the module. It can be either a "
"ParallelStyle object which contains how we prepare input/output for "
"Tensor Parallelism or it can be a dict of module FQN and its "
"corresponding ParallelStyle object. If not specified, the call will do "
"nothing at the moment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4147
msgid ""
"src_data_rank (int, optional) – the rank of the source data for the "
"logical/global tensor, it is used by distribute_tensor() to "
"scatter/broadcast the shards/replicas to other ranks. By default, we use "
"group_rank=0 on each DeviceMesh dimension as the source data to preserve "
"the single-device semantic. If passing None explicitly, "
"parallelize_module() simply uses its local data instead of trying to "
"preserve the single-device semantic via scatter/broadcast. Default: 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4149
msgid "A nn.Module object parallelized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4151
msgid ""
"For complex module architecture like Attention, MLP layers, we recommend "
"composing different ParallelStyles together (i.e. ColwiseParallel and "
"RowwiseParallel) and pass as a parallelize_plan, to achieves the desired "
"sharding computation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4153
msgid "Tensor Parallelism supports the following parallel styles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4155
msgid ""
"Partition a compatible nn.Module in a column-wise fashion. Currently "
"supports nn.Linear and nn.Embedding. Users can compose it together with "
"RowwiseParallel to achieve the sharding of more complicated modules. "
"(i.e. MLP, Attention)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4157
msgid ""
"input_layouts (Placement, optional) – The DTensor layout of input tensor "
"for the nn.Module, this is used to annotate the input tensor to become a "
"DTensor. If not specified, we assume the input tensor to be replicated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4159
msgid ""
"output_layouts (Placement, optional) – The DTensor layout of the output "
"for the nn.Module, this is used to ensure the output of the nn.Module "
"with the user desired layout. If not specified, the output tensor is "
"sharded on the last dimension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4161 ../../source/references_other.md:4173
msgid ""
"use_local_output (bool, optional) – Whether to use local torch.Tensor "
"instead of DTensor for the module output, default: True."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4163
msgid "A ParallelStyle object that represents Colwise sharding of the nn.Module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4165
msgid ""
"By default ColwiseParallel output is sharded on the last dimension if the"
" output_layouts not specified, if there’re operators that require "
"specific tensor shape (i.e. before the paired RowwiseParallel), keep in "
"mind that if the output is sharded the operator might need to be adjusted"
" to the sharded size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4167
msgid ""
"Partition a compatible nn.Module in a row-wise fashion. Currently "
"supports nn.Linear and nn.Embedding. Users can compose it with "
"ColwiseParallel to achieve the sharding of more complicated modules. "
"(i.e. MLP, Attention)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4169
msgid ""
"input_layouts (Placement, optional) – The DTensor layout of input tensor "
"for the nn.Module, this is used to annotate the input tensor to become a "
"DTensor. If not specified, we assume the input tensor to be sharded on "
"the last dimension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4171
msgid ""
"output_layouts (Placement, optional) – The DTensor layout of the output "
"for the nn.Module, this is used to ensure the output of the nn.Module "
"with the user desired layout. If not specified, the output tensor is "
"replicated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4175
msgid "A ParallelStyle object that represents Rowwise sharding of the nn.Module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4177
msgid ""
"SequenceParallel replicates a compatible nn.Module parameters and runs "
"the sharded computation with input sharded on the sequence dimension. "
"This currently supports nn.LayerNorm, nn.Dropout, and the RMSNorm python "
"implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4179
msgid ""
"This style implements the operation that is described in the paper "
"Reducing Activation Recomputation in Large Transformer Models"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4181
msgid ""
"If the input passed in to this nn.Module is a torch.Tensor, it assumes "
"that the input is already sharded on the sequence dimension and converts "
"the input to a DTensor sharded on the sequence dimension. If the input "
"passed in to this nn.Module is already a DTensor but is not sharded on "
"the sequence dimension, it would redistribute the input to be sharded on "
"the sequence dimension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4183
msgid "The output of the nn.Module will be sharded on the sequence dimension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4185
msgid ""
"sequence_dim (int, optional) – The sequence dimension of the input tensor"
" for the nn.Module, this is used to annotate the input tensor to become a"
" DTensor that is sharded on the sequence dimension, default: 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4187
msgid ""
"use_local_output (bool, optional) – Whether to use local torch.Tensor "
"instead of DTensor for the module output, default: False."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4189
msgid "A ParallelStyle object that represents Sequence Parallel of the nn.Module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4191
msgid ""
"SequenceParallel style assumes ones initialization if there are weights "
"in the nn.Module (i.e. nn.LayerNorm or RMSNorm, and they by default have "
"ones initialization). If you have custom inits for the weights on those "
"modules, you need to broadcast the weights before/after parallelizing to "
"ensure that they are replicated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4193
msgid ""
"To simply configure the nn.Module’s inputs and outputs with DTensor "
"layouts and perform necessary layout redistributions, without distribute "
"the module parameters to DTensors, the following ParallelStyle s can be "
"used in the parallelize_plan when calling parallelize_module:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4195
msgid ""
"Configure the nn.Module’s inputs to convert the input tensors of the "
"nn.Module to DTensors at runtime according to input_layouts, and perform "
"layout redistribution according to the desired_input_layouts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4197 ../../source/references_other.md:4221
msgid ""
"input_layouts (Union[Placement, Tuple[Optional[Placement]]]) – The "
"DTensor layouts of input tensors for the nn.Module, this is used to "
"convert the input tensors to DTensors. If some inputs are not "
"torch.Tensor or no need to convert to DTensors, None need to be specified"
" as a placeholder. default: None."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4199 ../../source/references_other.md:4223
msgid ""
"desired_input_layouts (Union[Placement, Tuple[Optional[Placement]]]) – "
"The desired DTensor layout of input tensors for the nn.Module, this is "
"used to ensure the inputs of the nn.Module have the desired DTensor "
"layouts. This argument needs to have the same length with input_layouts. "
"default: None."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4201 ../../source/references_other.md:4225
msgid ""
"input_kwarg_layouts (Dict[str, Placement]) – The DTensor layouts of input"
" kwargs for the nn.Module, this is used to convert the input kwarg "
"tensors to DTensors. default: None"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4203 ../../source/references_other.md:4227
msgid ""
"desired_input_kwarg_layouts – (Dict[str, Placement]): The desired DTensor"
" layout of input kwargs for the nn.Module, this is used to ensure the "
"inputs of the nn.Module have the desired DTensor layouts. default: None."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4205
msgid ""
"use_local_output (bool, optional) – Whether to use local torch.Tensor "
"instead of DTensor for the module inputs, default: False."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4207
msgid ""
"A ParallelStyle object that prepares the sharding layouts of the "
"nn.Module’s inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4209
msgid ""
"Configure the nn.Module’s outputs to convert the output tensors of the "
"nn.Module to DTensors at runtime according to output_layouts, and perform"
" layout redistribution according to the desired_output_layouts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4211 ../../source/references_other.md:4231
msgid ""
"output_layouts (Union[Placement, Tuple[Placement]]) – The DTensor layouts"
" of output tensors for the nn.Module, this is used to convert the output "
"tensors to DTensors if they are torch.Tensor. If some outputs are not "
"torch.Tensor or no need to convert to DTensors, None need to be specified"
" as a placeholder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4213 ../../source/references_other.md:4233
msgid ""
"desired_output_layouts (Union[Placement, Tuple[Placement]]) – The desired"
" DTensor layouts of output tensors for the nn.Module, this is used to "
"ensure the outputs of the nn.Module have the desired DTensor layouts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4215 ../../source/references_other.md:4235
msgid ""
"use_local_output (bool, optional) – Whether to use local torch.Tensor "
"instead of DTensor for the module outputs, default: True."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4217
msgid ""
"A ParallelStyle object that prepares the sharding layouts of the "
"nn.Module’s outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4219
msgid ""
"Configure the nn.Module’s inputs (and outputs) to convert the input "
"tensors (and output tensors, respectively) of the nn.Module to DTensors "
"at runtime according to input_layouts (and output_layouts, respectively),"
" and perform layout redistribution according to the desired_input_layouts"
" (and desired_output_layouts, respectively). This is a combination of "
"PrepareModuleInput and PrepareModuleOutput."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4229
msgid ""
"use_local_input (bool, optional) – Whether to use local torch.Tensor "
"instead of DTensor for the module inputs, default: False."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4237
msgid ""
"A ParallelStyle object that prepares the sharding layouts of the "
"nn.Module’s inputs and outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4239
msgid ""
"when using the Shard(dim) as the input/output layouts for the above "
"ParallelStyle s, we assume the input/output activation tensors are evenly"
" sharded on the tensor dimension dim on the DeviceMesh that TP operates "
"on. For instance, since RowwiseParallel accepts input that is sharded on "
"the last dimension, it assumes the input tensor has already been evenly "
"sharded on the last dimension. For the case of uneven sharded activation "
"tensors, one could pass in DTensor directly to the partitioned modules, "
"and use use_local_output=False to return DTensor after each "
"ParallelStyle, where DTensor could track the uneven sharding information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4241
msgid ""
"For models like Transformer, we recommend users to use ColwiseParallel "
"and RowwiseParallel together in the parallelize_plan for achieve the "
"desired sharding for the entire model (i.e. Attention and MLP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4243
msgid ""
"Parallelized cross-entropy loss computation (loss parallelism), is "
"supported via the following context manager:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4245
msgid ""
"A context manager that enables loss parallelism, where efficient "
"parallelized loss computation can be performed when the input is sharded "
"on the class dimension. Currently only the cross-entropy loss is "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4247
msgid ""
"Within this context manager, one can use cross_entropy() or "
"CrossEntropyLoss as usual, with the following assumptions on the input "
"parameters. The corresponding backward() call, if any, also needs to "
"happen under this context manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4249
msgid ""
"input (DTensor) – Input logits. Assumed to be sharded on the class "
"dimension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4251
msgid ""
"target (Union[torch.Tensor, DTensor]) – Must be ground truth class "
"indices (class probabilities currently not supported). Assumed to be "
"replicated across the DeviceMesh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4253
msgid ""
"weight (Union[torch.Tensor, DTensor], optional) – If given, assumed to be"
" replicated across the DeviceMesh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4255
msgid "label_smoothing – Currently not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4257
msgid "A replicated DTensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_other.md:4259
msgid ""
"A sharded DTensor is manually created here to showcase the usage. In "
"practice, it is usually the output of a TP module."
msgstr ""

